1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:07,985
Nesting packs every part onto sheets. Each sheet becomes one CNC program.

2
00:00:07,985 --> 00:00:11,471
The header shows the program name, material, sheet size (144 x 60 in), trim and spacing.

3
00:00:11,471 --> 00:00:16,598
The list on the left: every sheet, its material, part count and how full it is.

4
00:00:16,598 --> 00:00:23,589
Click any part to see what it is: cabinet, cut size, edges, cut order and label spot.

5
00:00:23,589 --> 00:00:28,301
Machining shows the holes on each part. Turn it off for a clean view of the layout.

6
00:00:28,301 --> 00:00:31,773
Area and cost: parts, kept offcuts and scrap per sheet and for the whole job.

7
00:00:31,773 --> 00:00:35,213
No price is invented: a material shows a Configure badge until you enter its price.

8
00:00:35,213 --> 00:00:39,287
Sheet checks list problems found on this sheet, the same ones the export check uses.

9
00:00:39,287 --> 00:00:45,473
Edit layout lets you move parts by hand. Open Sheet 3, the MDF doors.

10
00:00:45,473 --> 00:00:49,657
Drag a part. It snaps beside its neighbours, in line with edges, or to the trim.

11
00:00:49,657 --> 00:00:56,053
Turn rotates the selected part. The live check watches for overlaps and grain.

12
00:00:56,053 --> 00:01:00,729
Save layout keeps it with the job. Programs, labels and checks use the saved layout.
